    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOFpg0Ns8AAAABAfcieA",
      "title": "Add KNINE (K9 Finance DAO)",
      "author": "MRShimamoto",
      "number": 1351,
      "body": "KNINE is the governance token of K9 Finance DAO, the former liquid staking protocol for Shibarium, relaunched on Base after the 2025 Shibarium Bridge hack.\r\n\r\n**Addresses** — the same on both chains, deployed from one address at nonce 0 on each:\r\n\r\n| Chain | Address |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| ethereum | `0x91fbB2503AC69702061f1AC6885759Fc853e6EaE` |\r\n| base | `0x91fbB2503AC69702061f1AC6885759Fc853e6EaE` |\r\n\r\n`name`, `symbol` and `decimals` read back as `K9 Finance DAO` / `KNINE` / `18` on both chains.\r\n\r\n**Why `overrides.bridge` is set**\r\n\r\nThe Base deployment is an OptimismMintableERC20 on the standard `L2StandardBridge`. It exposes the current `bridge()` / `remoteToken()` pair rather than the legacy `l2Bridge()` / `l1Token()` getters the validator probes, so those calls revert and the check cannot read the bridge. The override carries the value `bridge()` actually returns on chain, `0x4200000000000000000000000000000000000010`, and `remoteToken()` returns the Ethereum address listed above.\r\n\r\n**Disclosure: KNINE charges a tax on DEX sells**\r\n\r\nRaising this directly rather than leaving it to be discovered. The token can charge a tax on buys or sells, with a maximum of 10% - only tiggered by transfers into a recognised UniswapV2-style pair. It is not a general fee-on-transfer token. Bridge paths are exempt by constructio.\r\n\r\nValidated locally with `npx tsx ./bin/cli.ts validate --datadir ./data --tokens KNINE`: no errors, one warning for the overridden bridge.\r\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/ethereum-optimism.github.io",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-21T01:45:59Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 385,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOFpg0Ns8AAAABAiNSJA",
      "title": "HRUSD: add token to Base",
      "author": "teamskew",
      "number": 1352,
      "body": "Adds HRUSD, a USD-pegged stablecoin issued natively on Base, to the Superchain token list.\n\nBase only — HRUSD is not deployed on any other chain and has no bridged supply, so this is a\nsingle-chain PR.\n\n### Token\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Address | `0x5587AD03F9565F1B86cfA51a3C744Bcc4039dAf0` |\n| Chain | Base |\n| Name / symbol | HRUSD / HRUSD |\n| Decimals | 6 |\n\n`name`, `symbol` and `decimals` in `data.json` were read from the contract on Base and match\nit exactly, so the on-chain consistency check should pass. The description is 233 characters,\nunder the 1000 limit.\n\n### Elsewhere\n\nHRUSD is listed on DeFiLlama, both as a protocol (`hrusd`, id 8458) and as a pegged asset\n(id 433, `peggedUSD`, crypto-backed). It is not on CoinGecko or CoinMarketCap.\n\n### Logo\n\n`logo.svg` is 256x256 with a transparent background and real vector paths — no embedded\nraster, no base64. Worth stating plainly: it was vectorised from the project's own PNG\nartwork rather than exported from a vector source, because no SVG original was available.\nThe outline was traced from the artwork, smoothed, and simplified to 84 vertices; measured\nagainst the source bitmap it reaches an IoU of 0.981, with the remainder being the antialiased\nedge of the original. The gradient was sampled along its own axis (#0744DC to #0FC3FA) and\nreproduced with three stops.\n\nThe source PNG is a horizontal lockup — brand mark plus wordmark, on an opaque white\nbackground — so only the square mark was taken, which is what a token icon calls for.\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/ethereum-optimism.github.io",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-21T10:05:05Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 25,
      "deletions": 0
    },
